with the allantois.

248
00:15:07,890 --> 00:15:10,450
Allantois is a structure
which helps the

249
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:14,450
embryo exchange gases
and handle liquid waste.

250
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:18,890
Anyway, allantois is closed
or obliterated at birth.

251
00:15:18,890 --> 00:15:22,870
If it remains open, it will
create a fistulos urinary

252
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:26,410
tract connection between the
bladder and the umbilicus.

253
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:30,610
This is illustrated
very nicely in these

254
00:15:30,610 --> 00:15:35,630
drawings. The left
side drawing shows an

255
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:39,310
uracus which is
connected to the bladder.

256
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:42,990
The patient in this
case will present with

257
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:46,450
abdominal pain and
drainage of fluid. The

258
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:49,350
right side drawing
shows an urechal cyst.

259
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:53,430
This cyst results
if only a central

260
00:15:53,430 --> 00:15:56,510
region of a patent
urechus remains.

261
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,310
This region is limited by

262
00:15:59,310 --> 00:16:01,870
segments of
obliterated urechus.

263
00:16:02,410 --> 00:16:05,750
This lesion is associated
with an increased

264
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:08,630
risk of transformation
into an adenocarcinoma.

265
00:16:10,450 --> 00:16:13,950
Aco-denchronic
cystitis. In general,

266
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,390
cystitis is very
important as it precedes

267
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:19,530
the bacterial
infection of kidney,

268
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:21,610
the bacterial pyelonephritis.

269
00:16:21,610 --> 00:16:25,410
In these cases, there
is retrograde spread of

270
00:16:25,410 --> 00:16:28,990
micro-organes from the
bladder all the way to

271
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:32,450
the kidneys and their
collecting systems. The

272
00:16:32,590 --> 00:16:36,070
most important predisposing
factors are the bladder

273
00:16:36,070 --> 00:16:38,850
calculi and the urinary
tract obstruction.

274
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:42,470
It is also seen frequently
in patients with

275
00:16:42,470 --> 00:16:46,810
diabetes mellitus and
immune deficiencies and may

276
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:49,910
appear iatrogenically
after instrumentation.

277
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:54,170
The most important
etiologic agents of

278
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:57,290
cystitis are the
coliforms, such as E.

279
00:16:57,290 --> 00:17:00,670
coli, Proteus, Klebsiola
and Enterobacter.

280
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:07,390
Also adenovirus mycosystitis
as well as mycoplasma.

281
00:17:08,070 --> 00:17:11,270
In some parts of the
world, for example in some

282
00:17:11,270 --> 00:17:14,950
African and Middle Eastern
countries, parasitic

283
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:18,950
flatworms such as
schizostoma determine a

284
00:17:18,950 --> 00:17:22,670
specific type of infection
called schistostomiasis,

285
00:17:22,990 --> 00:17:27,030
which is associated
with cystitis. I would

286
00:17:27,030 --> 00:17:29,430
like to mention that
each year, hundreds of

287
00:17:29,430 --> 00:17:33,350
millions are infected
with this parasite.

288
00:17:34,370 --> 00:17:35,650
Also,

289
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:38,070
a tuberculosis titus is seen

290
00:17:38,070 --> 00:17:39,810
after renal tuberculosis.

291
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:42,230
In addition,

292
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:46,350
candida and much less
frequent cryptococcus

293
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:50,590
mycosystitis in those receiving
long-term antibiotics.

294
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:53,370
Please note that, overall,

295
00:17:53,590 --> 00:17:56,750
women are more likely
to develop cystitis

296
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:59,420
as they have a
shorter urethra, which

297
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:01,570
facilitates the
spread of infection

298
00:18:03,230 --> 00:18:05,610
Acute cystitis morphology

299
00:18:06,650 --> 00:18:09,770
Microscopically, as you
may see on the left side

300
00:18:09,770 --> 00:18:13,710
image, acute cystitis is
characterized by hyperemia

301
00:18:13,710 --> 00:18:17,130
or congestion with small
focal hemorrhagic areas

302
00:18:17,530 --> 00:18:21,750
The right microphotograph
shows a tissue section

303
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:24,490
taken from a bladder
with acute cystitis.

304
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:28,230
There is an urotelial
ulceration and

305
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:30,350
massive inflammatory
infiltrate with

306
00:18:30,350 --> 00:18:33,530
neutrophils, eosinophils,
and lymphocytes.

307
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:37,230
There is also subepithelial
lymphoid follicle

308
00:18:37,230 --> 00:18:41,170
formation, indicating
that the patient has had

309
00:18:41,170 --> 00:18:44,010
an ongoing inflammation
for quite some time.

310
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,870
On this slide I have
inserted a set of

311
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:52,350
endoscopic images relevant
for chronic cystitis.

312
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:55,490
In all of these we'd
note the friable

313
00:18:55,490 --> 00:18:58,130
thin aspect of the
mucosa with mild

314
00:18:58,130 --> 00:19:01,650
congestion and in
some cases ulceration.

315
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:10,480
As you might see in this
micro photographs the

316
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:14,100
histological evaluation
of a bladder with chronic

317
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:17,620
inflammation, reveals
significant fibrosis

318
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:21,460
and a chronic inflammatory
infiltrate with osinophils,

319
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:24,620
lymphocytes, and
histiocytes present all

320
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:28,360
over the submucosa of
the urinary bladder wall.

321
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:35,560
Malachoplecae. This is a
form of chronic cystitis

322
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:38,560
associated with an abnormal
phygocytic function.

323
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:42,700
It is seen frequently in
renal transplants recipients

324
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:45,940
that develop chronic
bladder infections with

325
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:50,020
bacteria such as E. coli
and rarely with protease

326
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:54,220
It is accepted that as
a result of an abnormal

327
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:58,720
phygocytic function, the
macrophages cannot digest and

328
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:03,000
eliminate the microorganisms
The macrophages will appear

329
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:07,720
as large cells with
granulocytoplasm In addition,

330
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:11,920
calcium will be
accumulating within these

331
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:17,000
cells, and this deposit
will be easily identified

332
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,900
in histology as
Michaelis-Gutman bodies.

333
00:20:22,130 --> 00:20:25,620
Anyway, as you can see
in the left side image,

334
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:30,020
malachoplechia is characterized
by soft yellow raised

335
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:33,820
mucosal plaques of several
centimeters in diameter.

336
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:37,880
The right side histological
image shows a bladder

337
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:41,980
section with numerous
foamy granular macrophages

338
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:46,200
and lymphocytes. Some of
these cells present also

339
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:50,480
with obvious dark rounded
Michaelis-Goodman bodies.

340
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:57,020
Now I would like to
summarize the most important

341
00:20:57,020 --> 00:21:00,040
aethiopathogenic and
morphologic characteristics

342
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:03,100
related to obstruction
of the bladder outlet.

343
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:06,060
This is a very
important condition due

344
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:08,660
to its potential
effect on the kidneys.

345
00:21:09,850 --> 00:21:12,800
It is more common
in men and it is

346
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,820
caused by benign
prostatic hyperplasia.

347
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:19,660
It is less common in women
where it is frequently

348
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:22,560
determined by a
cystocyl of the bladder.

349
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:28,140
In some cases it is
determined by inflammatory or

350
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:32,260
congenital urethral strictures,
bladder tumors, bladder

351
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:35,620
obstruction caused by
foreign bodies and calculi.

352
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:39,380
It is also seen in
patients with neurogenic

353
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:42,120
bladder in which the
nerves controlling

354
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,880
the bladder contraction
are damaged.

355
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:48,420
Morphologically,
this condition is

356
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:50,720
characterized by
thickening of the bladder

357
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:53,740
wall due to smooth
muscle hypertrophy.

358
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:57,800
In long-standing cases,
as you might see in

359
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:01,200
this image, each
individual muscle fiber

360
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:04,560
bundles, increase
significantly in size, and

361
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:07,220
produce trabeculation
of the bladder wall.

362
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:12,220
Let's discuss now
a very important

363
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:14,760
topic, the
Eurotelial Neoplasms.

364
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:17,840
First of all, I would
like to mention that

365
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:20,480
bladder cancer is the
ninth most common cancer

366
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:23,600
type worldwide. It
is the fourth most

367
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:27,260
common cancer in American
men, and more than

368
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:31,800
95% of cases are
epithelial or transitional.

369
00:22:33,340 --> 00:22:36,720
Urothelial transitional
tumors may be non

370
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:39,960
-invasive and invasive
or infiltrating.

371
00:22:40,190 --> 00:22:42,820
Some patients might
present with other types

372
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:46,540
of cancers such as
adenocarcinoma, squamous

373
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:49,760
cell carcinoma, mixed
carcinoma, small

374
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:52,940
cell carcinoma, or
sarcoma of the bladder.

375
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,160
Eurotelial nerve
plus risk factors.

376
00:22:58,320 --> 00:23:02,440
The most important risk
factor is cigarette smoking,

377
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:06,160
which increases the risk
threefold to sevenfold.

378
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:09,160
Another risk factor
is the exposure to to

379
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:13,300
naphthalamine and other
arylamines in these patients,

380
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:16,720
cancer would appear 15 to 40

381
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:18,880
years after the
initial exposure.

382
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:21,420
Also, bladder cancer is

383
00:23:21,420 --> 00:23:23,700
associated with
schizostomiasis.

384
00:23:24,130 --> 00:23:28,330
This is endemic, as I mentioned
before, in northeastern

385
00:23:28,330 --> 00:23:32,720
Africa and Middle East,
and it seems that this

386
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:36,560
chronic cystitis induced
by schizostoma provides

387
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,880
an optimal environment for
epithelial dysplasia and

388
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:44,060
neoplasia. In this setting,
70% of these cancers are

389
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:48,800
squamous and 30% are
urotelial or adenocarcinoma.

390
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:54,520
In addition, urotelial
neoplasms of the bladder have

391
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:57,260
been reported after long
-term administration of

392
00:23:57,260 --> 00:24:01,220
analgesics, psychophosphamide,
and after irradiation.

393
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:07,520
Urotelial neoplasia
pathogenesis. So we have non

394
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:11,680
-invasive and invasive
cancers in the bladder. So

395
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:15,140
what's happening in one
setting versus the other?

396
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:16,580
Well,

397
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:20,040
molecular evaluation of
the non-invasive papillary

398
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:23,300
cancers has shown that
these lesions have an

399
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:26,800
amplification of the
fibroblast growth factor

400
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:31,400
receptor 3 tyrosine kinase
receptor gene, as well

401
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:36,080
as mutations in the
genes encoding RAS, rat

402
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:41,520
sarcoma virus and PI3,
phosphoenositide 3 kinase

403
00:24:42,350 --> 00:24:45,800
These tumors might recur
but as you may see in this

404
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:50,500
drawing these lesions become
invasive only if additional

405
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:53,860
genetic and epigenetic
abnormalities are induced

406
00:24:54,360 --> 00:25:00,180
This situation is described
in about 20% of cases On

407
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:03,680
the other hand, most of
the muscle-invasive bladder

408
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:08,660
cancers develop from a so
-called flat carcinoma in situ,

409
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:10,540
which is characterized by

410
00:25:10,540 --> 00:25:14,340
mutations of p53
and rb pathways.

411
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:19,080
In most of these cases,
other superimposed

412
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:21,920
genetic and epigenetic
changes develop

413
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:25,540
frequently, leading
to an invasive lesion.

414
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:29,160
These tumors are
considered high

415
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:31,590
grade as they are multifocal

416
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:38,540
In conclusion, the
non-invasive papillary

417
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:41,060
tumors are most common and some

418
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:44,100
might become invasive
On the other hand,

419
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:47,400
the initial non
-invasive flat carcinoma

420
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:50,440
in situ represents a
lesion with features

421
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:53,140
of malignancy confined
to the epithelium

422
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:56,220
It becomes frequently
metastatic as

423
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:59,500
numerous molecular
abnormalities coexist.

424
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:07,220
In terms of microscopic
appearance, urothelial

425
00:26:07,220 --> 00:26:10,040
cancers might be papillary,
nodular, or flat.

426
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:12,780
However, WHO and
the International

427
00:26:12,780 --> 00:26:16,420
Society of Urological
Pathology, ISUP,

428
00:26:16,470 --> 00:26:20,440
classifies this lesion
in flat and papillary

429
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:23,920
exophytic lesions.
Flat lesions include

430
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:26,440
urothelial proliferation
of uncertain

431
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:29,240
malignant potential,
or flat hyperplasia,

432
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,340
urothelial dysplasia,

433
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:34,850
and urothelial carcinoma
is such. Exophytic

434
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:39,860
papillary lesions are
represented by papilloma,

435
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,440
urotelial proliferation
of uncertain

436
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:45,740
malignant potential or
papillary hyperplasia,

437
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,660
papillary urotelial neoplasm

438
00:26:48,660 --> 00:26:50,420
of low malignant potential,

439
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:53,440
papillary urotelial carcinoma

440
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,400
low grade and high grade.

441
00:26:55,800 --> 00:26:58,420
It is beyond the scope
of today's lecture

442
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:01,480
to discuss all of
these in detail. We

443
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,820
will insist only on
the most important.

444
00:27:04,420 --> 00:27:07,800
The image on the right side

445
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:10,220
shows a cross-section bladder

446
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:13,320
in which the upper
part is remarkable

447
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:15,400
for a large papillary tumor,

448
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:18,480
while the lower
half shows several

449
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,680
brownish-gray papillary tumors.

450
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:26,720
The precise type of
this lesion is indicated

451
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:30,960
only after a
histopathological evaluation.

452
00:27:35,100 --> 00:27:37,640
Urotelial tumor histology.

453
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:39,600
Let's begin with papillomas.

454
00:27:39,910 --> 00:27:44,640
These represent 1% or less
of bladder cancers and

455
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:47,820
are seen in younger
patients. As noted on the

456
00:27:47,820 --> 00:27:51,120
left side image, they have
an exophytic finger-like

457
00:27:51,120 --> 00:27:55,180
structure with a central
fibrovascular core covered

458
00:27:55,180 --> 00:27:58,060
by an epithelium similar
to normal urotelium.

459
00:27:58,300 --> 00:28:01,980
Very rarely, these patients
would develop recurrences

460
00:28:01,980 --> 00:28:04,460
or progression after surgery.

461
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:09,200
Similar with papillomas
are the so-called papillary

462
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:12,820
urotelial neoplasm of
low malignant potential.

463
00:28:13,570 --> 00:28:16,780
However, as you might
see in the right side

464
00:28:16,780 --> 00:28:20,740
image, this lesion
presents with an

465
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:24,160
urotelium which is
thicker and has a greater

466
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:28,200
density of cells than
the regular papilloma.

467
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:31,800
In addition, they are
larger than the papillomas.

468
00:28:32,060 --> 00:28:38,000
However, as noted in
papillomas, progression is rare.

469
00:28:39,900 --> 00:28:44,220
On this slide we have on
the left side a microscopic

470
00:28:44,220 --> 00:28:49,120
image of a low-grade
and towards right we

471
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:52,300
have a high-grade urothelial
papillary carcinoma.

472
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:56,440
Low-grade papillary
urothelial carcinoma. These

473
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:59,520
lesions have a regular
or orderly pattern

474
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:03,200
and the cells are evenly
spaced and cohesive.

475
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:07,860
These cells present with
low-grade cytologic atipia,

476
00:29:07,860 --> 00:29:11,580
suggested by the presence
of hyperchromatic nuclei.

477
00:29:11,780 --> 00:29:14,540
These low-grade
lesions may recur

478
00:29:14,540 --> 00:29:17,560
and very rarely
became invasive.

479
00:29:18,350 --> 00:29:21,000
Compared with these
low-grade lesions in

480
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,080
high-grade popular
urothelial carcinoma,

481
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:27,700
there is disarray
and loss of polarity

482
00:29:27,700 --> 00:29:31,300
with these cohesive cells
and high-grade cytologic

483
00:29:31,300 --> 00:29:34,800
atipia, indicated by
the presence of large

484
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:40,100
hyperchromatic nuclei with
prominent nucleoli. You

485
00:29:40,100 --> 00:29:44,080
might also see atypical
mitosis in these cases.

486
00:29:44,540 --> 00:29:48,560
A significant number of
these lesions progress

487
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:52,640
to invasive bladder
cancer and metastasize to

488
00:29:52,640 --> 00:29:55,640
regional lymph nodes or
to the liver and lung.

489
00:29:57,800 --> 00:30:01,180
Carcinoma in sight, CIS.
This is a very important

490
00:30:01,180 --> 00:30:04,660
lesion as if left
untreated, it progresses to

491
00:30:04,660 --> 00:30:10,280
invasive cancer in 50 to 75
% of cases. On cystoscopy,

492
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:13,900
it appears as multifocal
areas of mucosal congestion,

493
00:30:13,900 --> 00:30:17,540
reddening, with granular
aspect or thickening,

494
00:30:17,540 --> 00:30:20,940
but without the presence
of an intraluminal mass.

495
00:30:21,590 --> 00:30:24,880
As you may note in this image,

496
00:30:25,140 --> 00:30:28,140
histologically, the atepia
involves the urotelium

497
00:30:28,140 --> 00:30:31,580
in its full thickness.
The cells are enlarged

498
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:35,260
with pleomorphic nuclei
and visible nucleoli.

499
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:39,840
In this setting, the
epithelial cells have lost

500
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:43,080
their cohesiveness and
might be shed in the urine.

501
00:30:45,540 --> 00:30:49,640
Now I would like to summarize
the invasive urotelial

502
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:53,640
carcinoma morphological
features by describing this

503
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:58,400
image. This image represents
