504
00:30:58,400 --> 00:31:03,600
The open bladder displays an
invasive urotelar carcinoma

505
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:08,860
with yellowish multinodular
masses filling most of

506
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:13,200
the bladder lumen. There
is ulceration and necrosis.

507
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:17,120
Please note that the most
important prognostic factor

508
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:21,340
in these patients with
invasive urotelial carcinoma

509
00:31:21,340 --> 00:31:26,020
is represented by the
stage. The stage is

510
00:31:26,020 --> 00:31:30,000
indicated by the depth of
invasion in the bladder wall.

511
00:31:30,420 --> 00:31:32,980
Invasion of the
muscularis propia

512
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:36,900
suggests radical cystectomy or

513
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:39,920
radiation therapy
or chemotherapy.

514
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:45,660
therapy. Well, it is
beyond the scope of today's

515
00:31:45,660 --> 00:31:49,520
lecture to discuss the primary
squamous and adenocarcinoma

516
00:31:49,520 --> 00:31:53,040
of the bladder. But before
we finish this section

517
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:56,460
on bladder, I would like to
mention that at this level

518
00:31:56,460 --> 00:32:01,000
there are secondary
malignant tumors. These are

519
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:05,560
metastases extending from
cervix, uterus, prostate, and

520
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:09,980
******. Also lymphoma might
