522
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:21,840
Pathology of the urethra.
Let's discuss the

523
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:25,780
inflammatory conditions
of urethra. So we have

524
00:32:25,780 --> 00:32:29,420
infectious and non
-infectious urethritis.

525
00:32:29,740 --> 00:32:33,720
There are two major types
of infectious urethritis,

526
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:36,460
gonococcal and non
-gonococcal urethritis.

527
00:32:36,660 --> 00:32:41,840
Gonococcal urethritis
indicates that the patient has

528
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:46,320
an early stage of this
sexual transmitted disease.

529
00:32:46,660 --> 00:32:50,600
Non-gonococcal
urethritis is caused by

530
00:32:50,600 --> 00:32:53,960
Chlamydia trachomatis
in up to 60% of cases

531
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:59,380
in men and in up to
20% of cases in women.

532
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:02,740
I would like to
highlight that infectious

533
00:33:02,740 --> 00:33:05,680
urethritis is
associated with cystitis

534
00:33:05,680 --> 00:33:08,680
in women and with
prostatitis in men.

535
00:33:09,520 --> 00:33:12,160
Some patients would
present with non

536
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:15,380
-infectious urethritis
in the context of

537
00:33:15,380 --> 00:33:18,320
reactive arthritis
or Reiter syndrome.

538
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:22,280
Reiter syndrome is a
triad which includes

539
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:25,660
arthritis, conjunctivitis
and urethritis.

540
00:33:26,220 --> 00:33:30,040
For information I have
included on this slide

541
00:33:30,040 --> 00:33:35,300
a cytological image which
represents the discharge

542
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:37,500
