of a patient with

543
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:40,740
gonorrhea. There are
numerous polymorphonuclear

544
00:33:40,740 --> 00:33:45,960
cells which have in their
cytoplasm diplococci

545
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:49,500
with a morphology suggestive
of Neisseria gonorrhea,

546
00:33:49,500 --> 00:33:53,820
so the patient has
gonococcal urethritis.

547
00:33:56,240 --> 00:34:00,180
Tumor-like lesions and
tumors of the urethra.

548
00:34:01,050 --> 00:34:03,400
First of all, I would
like to mention an

549
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:06,300
inflammatory lesion,
the urethral caruncle,

550
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:10,000
which may mimic an
ulcerated urethral tumor.

551
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:13,780
This presents as a
small red painful

552
00:34:13,780 --> 00:34:16,560
mass at the external
urethral meatus.

553
00:34:17,660 --> 00:34:21,380
Usually the patient is
an elderly female. It

554
00:34:21,380 --> 00:34:24,560
consists of inflamed
granulation tissue covered

555
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:27,720
by a friable mucosa
which might ulcerate.

556
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:31,820
Surgery is always the
therapy of choice.

557
00:34:33,970 --> 00:34:37,000
Now the most important
benign ureteral tumors

558
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:40,040
are the squamous and
urothelial papillomas,

559
00:34:40,510 --> 00:34:43,900
inverted urothelial
papillomas and condylomas.

560
00:34:44,220 --> 00:34:48,120
The left side microscopic
image represents

561
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:52,000
an inverted papilloma
which displace an

562
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:55,320
urotelium invaginating
into a lamina propria.

563
00:34:55,520 --> 00:34:58,680
This is patognom warning
for this condition.

564
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:05,620
The right side image
shows a polypoid lesion

565
00:35:05,620 --> 00:35:09,170
composed of hyperplastic
papillary fronds of

566
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:10,720
