567
00:35:11,340 --> 00:35:16,530
On high power in these
cases you might see cellular

568
00:35:16,530 --> 00:35:22,900
damage induced by HPV,
as this entity is caused

569
00:35:22,900 --> 00:35:27,940
by HPV, both low-risk
HPV and high-risk HPV.

570
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:34,420
Primary carcinoma of the
urethra. This is a very

571
00:35:34,420 --> 00:35:38,920
rare lesion, and it
represents 1% of all

572
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:42,200
urinary tract malignancies.
The most common type

573
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:46,100
are the urethelial and
squamous cell carcinoma.

574
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:51,260
The urethelial type is
most of the time seen

575
00:35:51,260 --> 00:35:54,060
in the proximal urethra,
while the squamous

576
00:35:54,060 --> 00:35:57,980
cell carcinoma and the
HPV related lesions are

577
00:35:57,980 --> 00:36:01,860
identified in the
distal urethra. Overall,

578
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:04,740
urethral carcinoma
is aggressive with a

579
00:36:04,740 --> 00:36:07,780
propensity for lymph
node and distant organ

580
00:36:07,780 --> 00:36:11,060
metastasis in the
lung, liver, and bone.

581
00:36:11,450 --> 00:36:13,500
Also, I would like
to mention that

582
00:36:13,610 --> 00:36:15,800
adenocarcinomas are
infrequent in the

583
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,880
urethra and generally
are seen in women.

584
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:24,860
The central microscopic image
shows a dissected urethra

585
00:36:24,860 --> 00:36:29,380
